{
  "id": "FRAME-3",
  "about": "p2p frame v3: one JSON object per line. Each frame of the registry's p2p table (op, dir) as module/p2p and tools/anetpeer write it, byte for byte; both read every line and write it back unchanged. Binary values are base64url without padding (core CORE-E5): the envelope here, and the dack (80 bytes, 107 characters), which only the recipient's daemon makes and everything between carries as it came. No frame says whether a message was processed or refused. The refused frames are answered with an error frame of v 3 (with the frame's id when it had one) and are never handed to a daemon or acked; a hello is also answered by closing the connection. Written by the Go test (go test ./module/p2p -run FRAME3 -update-frames).",
  "version": 3,
  "seeds": "every value below is SHA-256(\"anet-golden/v016/FRAME-3/<role>\"): envelope = H(envelope/0) || H(envelope/1), 64 bytes; dack = H(dack/0) || H(dack/1) || H(dack/2)[:16], 80 bytes. The AIDs are those of KEL-2B; the address is in 203.0.113.0/24 (RFC 5737).",
